CMD vs ADD — What’s the Difference in Docker? 

>CMD:-
	•Sets the default command to run when the container starts.
	•Commonly used to run applications or scripts.
	• Doesn’t create an extra layer in the Docker image.
Syntax: CMD ["python", "app.py"]

>ADD:-
	•Copies files or directories from the host into the Docker image.
	•Bonus: Can automatically extract compressed archives like .tar.gz.
	•Creates an extra layer in the image → can increase final image size.
Syntax: ADD app.tar.gz /app/

>Important Points :-
	•	Prefer using COPY instead of ADD unless you need advanced features.
	•	Use ADD only when you need archive extraction or want to fetch files from remote
